## Ki-Rin

A Ki-Rin is a divine beast, long-bodied and scaled: chitinous plates laid over a deer's frame, hooves, and a mouth of carnivorous teeth that slobbers gore. It breathes a rush of divine fire that can turn a crowd to ash, and calls up a deflecting wind to turn aside a blow.

The creature wears an aura of peace, and meeting its eyes shows an intelligence there that a person cannot bring themselves to snuff out. Those caught by it will not raise a hand against it while it lasts. It is no less deadly for that gentleness: one gored a guest to death on the Providence banquet floor, and another turned its fire on the guests after it was taken by mind magic.

Some came through a tear in the [[Phenomena/Weave|weave]] that opened over the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]]'s dance floor.
